From 4e8b017b1cbcd1de2185edc7b5375587a4184987 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Tatoh <tatukis@gmail.com>
Date: Fri, 18 Sep 2026 15:15:55 -0300
Subject: [PATCH 2/3] [es] AGREEMENT_POSTPONED_ADJ: keep the verb search inside
 the clause
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

Addresses the review on the previous commit: skip="-1" scans to the end of the
sentence, so a verb in a matrix clause satisfied the antipattern and suppressed
a real adjectival case in the subordinate one — «dice que la película más
seguido de la tele fue esa» was flagged before the antipattern and clean after.

An <exception scope="next"> on the skipped part stops the search at clause
boundaries. Adverbial uses are unaffected because the verb they need is in
their own clause: «quiero que vengas más seguido» still matches on «vengas».

A regression example is added for the subordinate case.

The reviewer's own example, «creo que la serie más seguido fue...», turns out
not to reproduce: it is clean with or without this rule change, so it is not
what the bound is for.

Re-measured on the same 810k-word corpus: still 21 matches, and the set is
byte-identical to the unbounded version, so the bound costs nothing on real
prose.
---
 .../main/resources/org/languagetool/rules/es/grammar.xml   | 7 +++++--
 1 file changed, 5 insertions(+), 2 deletions(-)

diff --git a/languagetool-language-modules/es/src/main/resources/org/languagetool/rules/es/grammar.xml b/languagetool-language-modules/es/src/main/resources/org/languagetool/rules/es/grammar.xml
index e9865191cba..9b5692b3acc 100644
--- a/languagetool-language-modules/es/src/main/resources/org/languagetool/rules/es/grammar.xml
+++ b/languagetool-language-modules/es/src/main/resources/org/languagetool/rules/es/grammar.xml
@@ -23598,8 +23598,10 @@ Foundation, Inc., 51 Franklin St, Fifth Floor, Boston, MA 02110-1301, USA
                 <!-- «más/menos seguido» with a verb in front is the adverbial
                      locution 'a menudo', invariable and general in the Americas.
                      Without a verb («la serie más seguido») it is still a
-                     postponed adjective and stays checked. -->
-                <token postag="V.*" postag_regexp="yes" skip="-1"/>
+                     postponed adjective and stays checked. The skipped part may
+                     not cross a clause boundary, so a verb in a matrix clause
+                     («dice que la película más seguido…») does not count. -->
+                <token postag="V.*" postag_regexp="yes" skip="-1"><exception scope="next" regexp="yes">que|quien|quienes|cual|cuales|cuando|donde|porque|aunque|,|;|:</exception></token>
                 <token regexp="yes">más|menos</token>
                 <token>seguido</token>
                 <example>Quiero pasear sin mi armadura más seguido.</example>
@@ -23649,6 +23651,7 @@ Foundation, Inc., 51 Franklin St, Fifth Floor, Boston, MA 02110-1301, USA
                 <example correction="posibles">De todas las maneras <marker>posible</marker>.</example>
                 <example correction="alta">Construyeron una torre bien <marker>alto</marker>.</example>
                 <example correction="seguida">La serie más <marker>seguido</marker>.</example>
+                <example correction="seguida">Dice que la película más <marker>seguido</marker> de la tele fue esa.</example>
                 <example>Uno de los aspectos migratorios más <marker>criticado</marker></example>
                 <example>con la bobina y la placa electrónica montadas en una caja única</example>
                 <example>El contacto con la cultura y la historia japonesas.</example>
